{"total_count": 7, "results": [{"visibility": "domain", "fields": [{"name": "type_of_central_heating_in_household", "description": null, "annotations": {"facet": true, "disjunctive": true, "sortable": true}, "label": "Type of central heating in household", "type": "text"}, {"name": "area", "description": null, "annotations": {"facet": true, "disjunctive": true, "sortable": true}, "label": "Area", "type": "text"}, {"name": "observation", "description": null, "annotations": {}, "label": "Observation", "type": "int"}, {"name": "proportion", "description": null, "annotations": {"unit": "%"}, "label": "Proportion", "type": "double"}], "dataset_id": "census-21-central-heating", "dataset_uid": "da_gbsi2x", "has_records": true, "features": ["analyze"], "attachments": [], "alternative_exports": [], "data_visible": true, "metas": {"default": {"title": "Census 21 - Central Heating", "description": "<p>The census is undertaken by the Office for National Statistics every 10 years and gives us a picture of all the people and households in England and Wales. The most recent census took place in March of 2021.</p><p>The census asks every household questions about the people who live there and the type of home they live in. In doing so, it helps to build a detailed snapshot of society. Information from the census helps the government and local authorities to plan and fund local services, such as education, doctors' surgeries and roads.</p><p>Key census statistics for Leicester are published on the open data platform to make information accessible to local services, voluntary and community groups, and residents. There is also a <a =""="" href="https://data.leicester.gov.uk/pages/census_leicester/" target=" _blank">dashboard</a> published showcasing various datasets from the census allowing users to view data for Leicester and compare this with national statistics.</p><p>Further information about the census and full datasets can be found on the ONS website - <a href="https://www.ons.gov.uk/census/aboutcensus/censusproducts" target="_blank">https://www.ons.gov.uk/census/aboutcensus/censusproducts</a><a href="https://www.ons.gov.uk/census/aboutcensus/censusproducts" target="_blank"></a></p><p><b>Central heating</b></p><p>This dataset provides Census 2021 estimates that classify occupied household spaces in England and Wales by the type of central heating present. The estimates are as at Census Day, 21 March 2021.<br/></p><p><b>Definition: </b>Central heating is a heating system used to heat multiple rooms in a building by circulating air or heated water through pipes to radiators or vents. Single or multiple fuel sources can fuel these systems.</p><p></p><p>Central heating systems that are unused or not working are still considered. No information is available for household spaces with no usual residents.</p><p>This dataset includes details for Leicester city and England overall.</p>", "theme": ["Population and Communities"], "keyword": ["Census", "Housing", "Central Heating"], "license": "Open Government Licence v3.0", "license_url": "http://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/", "language": "en", "modified": "2026-06-17T14:54:06.985000+00:00", "publisher": "Leicester City Council", "references": "https://www.ons.gov.uk/census/aboutcensus/censusproducts", "attributions": ["Office for National Statistics"], "update_frequency": null, "bbox": null, "data_processed": "2023-03-17T11:48:58.858000+00:00", "federated": false, "geographic_reference": ["uk_70_e06000016"], "geographic_reference_auto": true, "geometry_types": null, "metadata_languages": ["en"], "metadata_processed": "2026-06-17T14:54:09.425000+00:00", "modified_updates_on_data_change": true, "modified_updates_on_metadata_change": true, "parent_domain": null, "records_count": 24, "shared_catalog": null, "source_dataset": null, "source_domain": null, "source_domain_address": null, "source_domain_title": null, "territory": ["Leicester"], "timezone": null}, "inspire